  "fieldNotes": {
    "truckGate": "Single controlled truck entrance off 300 South on the north side; wide paved throat funnels trucks to a manned gatehouse with a red canopy spanning the drive (visible in 2021-05 inner-yard Street View). Perimeter chain-link fencing confirmed.",
    "guardShack": "Canopied check-in gatehouse in the entry throat with trucks queued at it; corroborated by published driver procedure (check in, receive a pager with the unload door number).",
    "remoteGs": "False because the gate IS manned with a physical check-in booth, not a kiosk.",
    "shipRcvSeparate": "Cross-dock: continuous dock-door rows on BOTH long faces (east and west) of the building; inbound and outbound run from physically separate dock banks.",
    "dockDoors": "Both long faces are packed with dock doors for ~640m; west-face Street View shows a continuous wall of dock seals. Easily 50+; ~180 total is an honest overhead estimate across both faces.",
    "dropArea": "Extensive trailer drop yards: a large east-side lot full of parked trailers, a north drop yard along 300 South, and a west-side yard. 50+ band.",
    "fastLaneOpportunity": "Very wide entrance apron with multiple truck-widths of unused paved room at the gate; physical space to add an express/bypass lane.",
    "entryLanes": "Estimated from the wide throat (~2 effective lanes inbound past the gatehouse); not lane-striped at the road.",
